WITH ins AS (INSERT INTO sais_resource_deadlines (resource_id, appeal_deadline, continued_benefits_deadline, hearing_request_deadline, reconsideration_deadline, judicial_review_deadline, source_file, source_hash8) VALUES 
('SAIS-PS-009-03', 'Appeal of a determination: both parties have an equal right. Institution-specific and SHORT, commonly 5-15 BUSINESS DAYS from the written outcome. Calendar it the day the notice arrives.', 'Supportive measures continue during the grievance process and during any appeal. If they lapse when the process concludes and you still need them, request continuation in writing.', 'There is generally no deadline to file a formal complaint under Title IX while you remain a student or participant, but evidence and witness memory degrade -- and the 180-day OCR clock runs independently.', 'Grounds for appeal are typically limited to procedural irregularity, new evidence not reasonably available at the time, or conflict of interest or bias. Frame the appeal in those terms explicitly.', 'ED Office for Civil Rights complaint: generally 180 DAYS from the last act of discrimination. A pending campus process does NOT toll this. File with OCR in parallel if you are approaching the deadline.', 'luminari-SAIS-ALL-RECORDS-2026.csv', 'fb433b18'),
('SAIS-PS-009-04', 'Not an appeal posture. Evidence lost to time or overwriting is generally unrecoverable, which is why preservation requests are the first action rather than a later one.', 'A non-report or anonymous kit is held for a statutory period -- commonly measured in years in many states -- preserving your ability to decide later. Ask how long your state holds it and calendar the expiration.', 'Forensic exam: most productive within roughly 72-120 hours by jurisdiction, but seek care regardless of elapsed time. Ask the local rape crisis center to send an advocate -- free, and available in most areas at any hour.', 'Request in writing that the school preserve surveillance video, card-access logs, and any incident reports. These are typically overwritten in 7-30 DAYS and the school will not preserve them unprompted.', 'Criminal limitations periods for sexual assault vary widely by state and have been extended substantially in many. A delayed report does not necessarily foreclose prosecution -- verify rather than assuming.', 'luminari-SAIS-ALL-RECORDS-2026.csv', 'fb433b18'),
('SAIS-PS-009-05', 'IDEA due process complaint: generally 2 YEARS from when the parent knew or should have known. State complaint to the education agency: generally 1 YEAR. OCR complaint: generally 180 DAYS. Three different clocks, all running at once.', 'STAY PUT: once a due process complaint is filed under IDEA, the child generally remains in the current educational placement during proceedings unless the parties agree otherwise. This is a powerful and widely unknown protection.', 'MANIFESTATION DETERMINATION REVIEW: required within 10 SCHOOL DAYS of a decision to change placement for disciplinary reasons. Request it in writing immediately -- it is the gate to challenging a disability-related suspension or expulsion.', 'Request an IEP or 504 team meeting in writing; districts must generally convene within a defined period set by state rule. Where a request is refused, the refusal must be given in writing as prior written notice.', 'State anti-bullying investigation timelines are commonly 5-10 SCHOOL DAYS with written notice of outcome to parents. Where the district misses it, escalate to the state education agency citing the statute.', 'luminari-SAIS-ALL-RECORDS-2026.csv', 'fb433b18'),
('SAIS-PS-009-06', 'OCR: generally 180 DAYS from the last discriminatory act. Private Title IX suit: generally the state''s personal injury period, commonly 1-4 years. Protective order denial: commonly 30 days, though refiling is usually faster.', 'A civil protection order can issue in a day and does not depend on any campus outcome. A campus no-contact directive is administrative and NOT enforceable by police -- know which one you have.', 'OCR complaints may be filed while a campus process is pending, and should be where the 180-day deadline is approaching. OCR may hold the complaint pending the school''s process, but the filing preserves your date.', 'Where OCR declines or dismisses, request the basis in writing. A private Title IX suit remains available and is not conditioned on an OCR finding.', 'Prior complaints about the same person held by the school are frequently the most valuable evidence in an institutional claim. Send a written PRESERVATION DEMAND naming the investigation file, prior reports, video, and card-access logs.', 'luminari-SAIS-ALL-RECORDS-2026.csv', 'fb433b18'),
('SAIS-PS-010-01', 'OSHA whistleblower retaliation complaint: 30 DAYS from the retaliatory act under section 11(c). This is one of the shortest federal deadlines anywhere and it is missed constantly. Other statutes administered by OSHA carry longer windows -- 180 days or more.', 'Report the hazard to the employer IN WRITING before or at the time of any refusal, and keep a copy. The refusal right requires that the employer was asked to correct the danger and did not.', 'OSHA complaint requesting an INSPECTION: file at any time; there is no deadline to report a hazard. Request that your name be kept CONFIDENTIAL -- OSHA will not disclose the complainant''s identity to the employer if you ask.', 'Where the employer has an internal reporting or threat assessment process, use it AND report externally. Internal reporting alone leaves no independent record and is frequently where complaints disappear.', 'Where injury occurred, a workers'' compensation claim has its own and often much shorter notice requirement -- commonly 30 DAYS to notify the employer. See the workers'' compensation section.', 'luminari-SAIS-ALL-RECORDS-2026.csv', 'fb433b18'),
('SAIS-PS-010-02', 'Contesting an OSHA outcome is generally the employer''s right, not the complainant''s. Where OSHA declines to inspect or closes without citation, request an INFORMAL CONFERENCE and, in writing, the basis for the decision.', 'Where the hazard is ongoing, request an inspection rather than only a phone or letter response. Ask explicitly for an ON-SITE INSPECTION and explain why a paper response is insufficient.', 'OSHA complaint: no deadline to file. Where you want an inspection, say so and provide specifics -- dates, locations, prior incidents, and what the employer was told and when.', 'Request the employer''s WORKPLACE VIOLENCE PREVENTION PROGRAM, hazard assessment, incident log, and training records. In states that mandate them, the absence of these documents is itself the violation.', 'Judicial review of final OSHA orders runs through the Occupational Safety and Health Review Commission and then the courts of appeals -- generally initiated by the employer or the Secretary, not the complainant.', 'luminari-SAIS-ALL-RECORDS-2026.csv', 'fb433b18'),
('SAIS-PS-010-03', 'OSHA section 11(c) retaliation: 30 DAYS from the retaliatory act. EEOC: 180 days, or 300 with concurrent state jurisdiction. NLRB: 6 months. State whistleblower statutes: commonly 1-3 years. FILE THE 30-DAY ONE FIRST.', 'Where you are still employed, document contemporaneously and preserve copies of your personnel file, performance reviews, schedules, and communications BEFORE any separation -- access is routinely cut off the day of termination.', 'OSHA will investigate and may seek reinstatement and back pay. Ask about REINSTATEMENT explicitly where you were terminated; it is available and rarely requested.', 'Where OSHA dismisses a section 11(c) complaint, ask for the basis in writing. Note that many state whistleblower statutes remain available with far longer deadlines even after a federal dismissal.', 'AFTER AN EEOC RIGHT-TO-SUE NOTICE: 90 DAYS TO FILE IN COURT. State whistleblower and wrongful discharge claims run on their own periods, commonly 1-3 years.', 'luminari-SAIS-ALL-RECORDS-2026.csv', 'fb433b18'),
('SAIS-PS-010-04', 'State fair employment agency complaint where survivor-status discrimination is barred: commonly 180 days, or 300 where concurrent with EEOC. Unemployment denial appeals are much shorter, commonly 10-30 days.', 'Request accommodations IN WRITING and keep the response. A documented request that goes unanswered is the foundation of both the safety claim and any later discrimination claim.', 'Protective order hearing: if a temporary order issued, the full hearing is commonly 10-21 days out and the temporary order DISSOLVES if you do not appear. See the Emergency Protective Order pipeline.', 'Where an accommodation is refused, ask for the refusal and its reason in writing, then file with the state labor department or fair employment agency. Refusal to engage is itself frequently actionable.', 'When filing for unemployment after leaving for safety reasons, STATE THE DOMESTIC VIOLENCE REASON EXPLICITLY on the claim. Most states treat it as good cause, which preserves eligibility that a bare quit would forfeit.', 'luminari-SAIS-ALL-RECORDS-2026.csv', 'fb433b18'),
('SAIS-PS-010-05', 'Workers'' compensation claim denial: administrative appeal to the state board, commonly 30-90 days from the denial notice. These deadlines are firm and short -- calendar them on receipt.', 'Where benefits are being terminated or reduced, request a hearing BEFORE the termination date where your state permits benefits to continue pending review. Ask the board what its rule is.', 'NOTICE TO THE EMPLOYER: commonly 30 DAYS from the injury, in writing. This is the deadline most often missed. Formal claim filing with the state board: commonly 1-2 years.', 'Where a claim is denied on the personal-assault exception, request reconsideration and argue that employment CONDITIONS contributed -- public access, known schedule, prior notice to the employer, or inadequate security.', 'Judicial review of a final board decision: state-specific, commonly 30 days. Note that workers'' compensation is generally the exclusive remedy against the EMPLOYER, but claims against a THIRD PARTY remain available.', 'luminari-SAIS-ALL-RECORDS-2026.csv', 'fb433b18'),
('SAIS-PS-010-06', 'EEOC: 180 days, or 300 with concurrent state jurisdiction. NLRB: 6 MONTHS. Union grievance: contract-specific and frequently only DAYS -- read the contract immediately. Third-party civil claims: commonly 1-3 years.', 'SEND THE EVIDENCE PRESERVATION DEMAND NOW to the employer, the property owner, and any security contractor. Video, access logs, and prior complaint files are the core of a premises case and are retained for weeks.', 'AFTER AN EEOC RIGHT-TO-SUE NOTICE: 90 DAYS TO FILE IN COURT. This is the most commonly blown deadline in employment law -- docket it the day the notice arrives.', 'Where a union grievance deadline has passed, ask about the duty of fair representation and whether the union will pursue it out of time. Separately, an NLRB charge has its own 6-month clock.', 'Where the employer is a government entity, a NOTICE OF CLAIM deadline as short as 30 DAYS may apply before any suit is possible. Determine this on day one.', 'luminari-SAIS-ALL-RECORDS-2026.csv', 'fb433b18'),
('SAIS-PS-011-01', 'Not an appeal posture. Evidence lost to deletion, platform removal, or retention expiry is generally unrecoverable -- there is no appeal from deleted data.', 'CAPTURE BEFORE YOU BLOCK OR REPORT. This single sequencing rule prevents most self-inflicted evidence loss in this pipeline.', 'Where an account is likely to be deleted or the person is likely to delete content, capture immediately -- within hours. Deleted platform content is frequently retained by the provider but only reachable through legal process, and only if it has not aged out.', 'Where you have already lost content to a platform removal, ask law enforcement to send a PRESERVATION REQUEST to the provider. Removed content is often still held on the provider''s systems for a period.', 'Federal law permits providers to be required to preserve records pending legal process for a defined period, extendable on request. This is initiated by law enforcement, which is why asking for it explicitly matters.', 'luminari-SAIS-ALL-RECORDS-2026.csv', 'fb433b18'),
('SAIS-PS-011-02', 'Not an appeal posture for a victim. Where a prosecutor declines, request the declination in writing and ask the victim-witness unit what additional evidence would change the decision.', 'Continue capturing and reporting. Federal cyberstalking is a COURSE OF CONDUCT offense -- the accumulation is the case, and each additional documented incident strengthens it.', 'Report to IC3 promptly. Federal and state limitations periods vary, but the practical deadline is provider retention -- records age out long before any statute does.', 'If local law enforcement says online conduct is not a crime or is ''a civil matter,'' ask for a supervisor, cite 18 U.S.C. sec. 2261A(2), and file with IC3 independently. Local declination does not bind federal authorities.', 'State cyberstalking limitations periods vary. Civil claims -- intentional infliction of emotional distress, defamation, invasion of privacy, and statutory image-abuse claims -- run on their own state periods, commonly 1-3 years.', 'luminari-SAIS-ALL-RECORDS-2026.csv', 'fb433b18'),
('SAIS-PS-011-03', 'Platform appeal of a rejected report: platform-specific, commonly available for a short window from the decision. Appeal it, and refile with the more specific policy category and quoted policy language.', 'Blocking may stop your view of the conduct without stopping the conduct. Consider capturing regularly from a monitored account or asking a trusted person to monitor rather than going blind to escalation.', 'For intimate images, submit to StopNCII.org (adults) or NCMEC Take It Down (anyone under 18 in the image) immediately -- proactive hash-matching prevents redistribution rather than chasing it.', 'Where a report is rejected, escalate through an advocacy organization with platform contacts. The Cyber Civil Rights Initiative Crisis Helpline at 844-878-2274 is free and does exactly this.', 'Search engine deindexing requests are separate from platform removal and should be filed in addition to it, not instead. Removing the search result limits reach even where the source page persists.', 'luminari-SAIS-ALL-RECORDS-2026.csv', 'fb433b18'),
('SAIS-PS-011-04', 'Federal civil action for nonconsensual disclosure of intimate images: generally 10 years from the later of the disclosure or the plaintiff reaching majority. State claims are commonly shorter -- verify separately.', 'Submit to StopNCII or Take It Down immediately and in parallel with reporting. Hash-matching prevents redistribution going forward, which is the harm that otherwise recurs indefinitely.', 'Report each impersonation account under the IMPERSONATION policy rather than harassment -- it is generally the faster removal path and does not require establishing a course of conduct.', 'For doxxed information, file opt-out and removal requests with data brokers and people-search sites directly. Several states require removal on request; most brokers honor opt-outs regardless of state.', 'State civil claims -- intentional infliction of emotional distress, invasion of privacy, defamation, and statutory image-abuse claims -- commonly run 1-3 years. The federal image action is substantially longer.', 'luminari-SAIS-ALL-RECORDS-2026.csv', 'fb433b18'),
('SAIS-PS-011-05', 'Not an appeal posture. Unauthorized account access and unauthorized tracking are separately criminal -- report them as their own offenses in addition to the stalking conduct.', 'DO NOT LOCK EVERYTHING DOWN BEFORE THE PLAN IS IN PLACE. Coordinate the change with a safety plan and, where applicable, with the timing of a protective order.', 'Where spyware or a tracker is suspected, do NOT remove it before consulting law enforcement and an advocate. Removal destroys forensic evidence and announces discovery.', 'After remediation, re-audit in 30 days. Access frequently re-establishes through a channel missed the first time, most often a recovery setting or a shared plan.', 'Federal offenses may apply to unauthorized access, interception, and interstate electronic stalking. Report to the FBI or IC3 in addition to local law enforcement.', 'luminari-SAIS-ALL-RECORDS-2026.csv', 'fb433b18'),
('SAIS-PS-011-06', 'Appeal of a denied protection order petition: state-specific, commonly 30 days. Refiling with the full captured record is usually faster and more effective. Title IX outcomes have institution-set appeal windows, commonly 5-15 business days.', 'THE TEMPORARY ORDER DISSOLVES IF YOU DO NOT APPEAR at the full hearing, commonly 10-21 days out. Calendar it the moment the temporary order issues.', 'Title IX SUPPORTIVE MEASURES are available immediately and do not require a formal complaint or a police report. Request them by name and in writing.', 'Where the person is anonymous, ask about filing against an unnamed defendant to obtain subpoena power for identification. This is the standard route and is frequently not mentioned.', 'Crime victim compensation: commonly 1-3 years to apply with a shorter reporting requirement, often 72 hours to 5 days, with good-cause exceptions. Federal image-abuse civil claims run substantially longer.', 'luminari-SAIS-ALL-RECORDS-2026.csv', 'fb433b18')
ON CONFLICT (resource_id) DO NOTHING RETURNING resource_id) SELECT count(*) AS inserted FROM ins